1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,992
My mother walks with three distinct shadows tonight, and absolutely none of them match her standing body on this street.

2
00:00:08,292 --> 00:00:18,900
Every single time we pass beneath a flickering streetlight, those dark silhouettes stretch across wet asphalt like desperate, reaching hands.

3
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:26,784
I already knew about the city's illegal shadow trade, where desperate people sell off pieces of their souls for cash.

4
00:00:27,084 --> 00:00:36,012
I honestly believed Mom was selfish. I thought she bought extra silhouettes to absorb her own relentless, crippling joint pain.

5
00:00:36,312 --> 00:00:43,680
So late tonight, while she slept on our worn couch, I finally pried open the heavy locked journal in her coat.

6
00:00:43,980 --> 00:00:53,436
The ink-stained pages weren't financial receipts. They were old hospital records for three unborn children she lost long ago.

7
00:00:53,736 --> 00:01:02,568
My lungs shattered on the final entry: three lost souls permanently tethered together just to power one dying baby girl.

8
00:01:02,868 --> 00:01:11,076
Terrified, I backed out the front door and stepped directly into the glaring yellow beam of the overhead streetlamp.

9
00:01:11,376 --> 00:01:19,032
I looked down at the rain-slicked concrete pavement. I didn't cast a single shadow of my own; I never had.

10
00:01:19,332 --> 00:01:27,876
When you walk home beneath the glowing streetlamps tonight, how many stolen shadows are secretly keeping your cold heart beating?
